==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sem-}}
{{etydate|1652}}; {{bor+|en|la|simulātus}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|simulō||make like, imitate, copy, represent, feign}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=verb|pos1=verb-forming suffix}}), from {{m|la|similis||like}}. See {{m|en|similar}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪm.jʊˌleɪt/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-simulate.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪm.jəˌleɪt/|a=US,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪm.jʊˌlæɪt/|a=AU}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To [[model]], [[replicate]], duplicate the behavior, appearance or properties of.
#: {{ux|en|We will use a smoke machine to '''simulate''' the fog you will actually encounter.}}
#: {{ux|en|This video game '''simulates''' a pinball machine.}}

